# Session: 2026-05-13

**Started:** ~05:30 UTC (resumed from previous day's PR #23 merge)
**Last Updated:** ~17:36 UTC (Dubai local 21:36)
**Project:** SandyStudio webapp — `claude/quizzical-brown-462555` worktree
**Topic:** E20 episode partial recovery + VGEN/STITCH/Realtime push fix pack (10+ patches, 2 migrations applied)

---

## What We Are Building

SandyStudio is an AI-first animation production studio. Today's session was a continuous Mode 2.5 production push to drive episode SS-S14-E20 ("The Violet Distance") from script-approved state through full Animator pipeline to a final cut mp4. Director worked through PA (Polina, gpt-5.5 in webapp) while I (Claude Code in terminal) handled code fixes.

The session evolved into a long sequence of pipeline issues surfaced by actual production usage:
- EREF prompt builder ignored storyboard camera intent → flat plate refs
- VGEN duration logic crashed with fractional/out-of-bounds values
- Veo 3.1 img2vid Standard tier only returns 8s clips (Google's error message misleads)
- Supabase Realtime push silent because RLS blocked anon channel subscriptions
- ffmpeg `-shortest` + short music loop truncated final cut to music duration
- ffmpeg concat played full mp4 durations, ignoring animatic shot_list timing
- Browser WebSocket leak зомбировал next-dev twice (2-5GB heap)
- Composer fix needed cross-worktree merge

Result: E20 closed partial (17/19 shots — SC11-SH01 + SC11-SH02 unreachable on Veo daily quota). Final cut mp4 exists at 96s (concat actual durations). All fixes committed via auto-sync. Pending: per-shot trim ffmpeg (q1), Postgres trigger Realtime (q2), team-chat unified channel (q3).

