## What Has NOT Been Tried Yet

### q1 — STITCH per-shot trim ✂️ (~30-45 min, planned)
Switch concat-list builder in `webapp/lib/agents/providers/ffmpeg-stitch.ts` from listing each shot with default duration to using ffmpeg concat demuxer's `inpoint`/`outpoint` directives:
```
file 'shot1.mp4'
outpoint 4
file 'shot2.mp4'
outpoint 5
```
Per-shot duration comes from `animatic_v1.shot_list[i].duration_seconds`. After patch, re-fire STITCH event — final cut should produce 54s correctly. Unit tests in `ffmpeg-stitch.test.ts` will need an update for the new args shape.

### q2 — Postgres trigger Realtime reliable 🔔 (~30 min, planned)
Browser-side Realtime push remains silent despite migration 0027. Replace fragile client subscription with server-side Postgres trigger:
```sql
CREATE FUNCTION trg_inject_ambient_turn() RETURNS trigger AS $$
BEGIN
  INSERT INTO concierge_turns (thread_id, role, event_type, content, metadata, created_at)
  SELECT id, 'system', 'message',
         format('[ambient pipeline event · %s] %s (actor=%s)',
                NEW.event_type, NEW.title, COALESCE(NEW.actor, 'system')),
         jsonb_build_object('kind','pipeline_event','activity_event_id',NEW.id, /*...*/),
         NEW.created_at
  FROM concierge_threads
  WHERE director_id = ... -- resolve from active session
    AND ended_at IS NULL
  ORDER BY started_at DESC LIMIT 1;
  RETURN NEW;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;

CREATE TRIGGER on_activity_event_insert AFTER INSERT ON activity_events
  EXECUTE FUNCTION trg_inject_ambient_turn();
```
Migration 0028. Need to resolve `thread_id` lookup — perhaps via `app_config` "active_thread:<director_id>" set on chat creation. After trigger lands, `useActivityRealtime.ts` becomes optional and can be simplified or removed.

### q3 — Team-chat unified channel 💬 (~50 min, planned, Director's directive)
Director wants minimal version: shared PA chat thread with all three participants writing.
- `POST /api/team-chat/post` — endpoint Claude posts via curl. Persists `role=system content="**Клод:** ..." metadata.kind='claude_message'`.
- `ConciergePanel.tsx` renders `kind='claude_message'` system turns as distinct bubble (e.g. blue, "Клод:" label).
- New PA system prompt block — lifts `kind='claude_message'` turns into her LLM context (similar to PIPELINE_EVENTS_SINCE_LAST_REPLY).
- Я post via Bash `curl` after every significant action.
- Director writes в его field в webapp → "Директор:". Я в том же thread через curl → "Клод:". PA отвечает в том же thread.

### q4 — E20 publish decision
Current final-cut.mp4 = 96s. Options:
- (a) Approve as-is and publish — 96s of full Veo content
- (b) Wait q1 fix → re-stitch 54s → approve → publish
- (c) Wait Veo daily quota recovery (next session?) → generate SC11-SH01 + SC11-SH02 → re-trim animatic to 19 shots → re-stitch full episode

