## Decisions Made

- **Force `durationSeconds=8` для Veo Standard + img2vid** — reason: Veo 3.1 docs confirmed img2vid Standard returns only 8s clips. Sending 5/6/7 returns 400. Trade-off: video timing diverges from storyboard intent (3-5s shots become 8s), so final cut needs per-shot trim in STITCH (q1 pending).
- **Singleton browser Supabase client** — reason: prevents WebSocket leak that turned next-dev into 2-5GB zombie. Module-level cache, no API change to callers.
- **RLS policy for Realtime — `TO authenticated USING (true)`** — reason: SandyStudio is single-director (per webapp.md §2.1). Every authenticated session belongs to Director. No multi-tenant boundary inside activity_events. Permissive SELECT is correct and minimal.
- **Drop role label + Beat:/Mood: in Veo prompt** — reason: Veo printed these as on-screen text annotations. The EREF already encodes framing/role.
- **Force 16:9 native composition prompt** — reason: Director observed videos starting as 1:1 inside 16:9 canvas then expanding mid-shot. Explicit "16:9 widescreen composition from the very first frame" instruction added.
- **Close E20 partial at 17/19 (animatic trim)** — reason: Director's "ждать бесполезно" after Veo daily quota exhausted on SC11-SH01 + SC11-SH02. Pipeline must move; SC11 punchlines were closing-act content but episode's narrative arc survives without them.
- **Two separate quality tier buttons (Fast / Standard)** — reason: Director needs to bypass Fast 429 quota explicitly. Single button defaulted to Fast and stuck there silently.
- **`-stream_loop -1` for ffmpeg music** — reason: Better default than `-shortest`-only because Director will often upload short loop files. Music behaves as infinite stream; video duration anchors the cut.
- **Backfill script over Realtime hot-fix** — reason: Realtime push debug requires browser-side investigation (DevTools, WebSocket frames). Faster recovery for current session via service-role backfill. Permanent fix shifted to q2 Postgres trigger.
- **Use existing `concierge_threads.bdbdafcf...` for team-chat (q3)** — reason: Director's PA thread is the canonical channel. New `role='system'` turns with `metadata.kind='claude_message'` don't require schema migration.
- **/clear before doing q1+q2+q3** — reason: context is deep; non-trivial multi-file changes risk bug surface if context runs out mid-fix. Fresh session better.

